1
00:00:00,385 --> 00:00:06,352
Meet Alex. Alex wants help booking a visit at Harbor Care, without exposing
another

2
00:00:06,422 --> 00:00:11,542
patient's information. The agent under test is the Patient Access Assistant.

3
00:00:11,983 --> 00:00:17,103
We will explain its tools and decision flow, test it in Rook's interactive
terminal,

4
00:00:17,312 --> 00:00:20,772
then inspect the same run in the hosted web interface.

5
00:00:21,283 --> 00:00:26,322
The customer data and business systems in this demonstration are fictional.

6
00:00:28,396 --> 00:00:32,831
The patient tool reads only the authenticated patient's record.

7
00:00:33,157 --> 00:00:38,068
Booking checks ownership and available slot capacity before reserving a
visit.

8
00:00:38,184 --> 00:00:41,133
Human escalation records an urgent handoff.

9
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:44,638
Record export is restricted to the customer portal.

10
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:50,153
Guidance supplies administrative information, with imported notes treated as

11
00:00:50,269 --> 00:00:55,656
untrusted content. These responsibilities keep scheduling separate from
clinical

12
00:00:55,703 --> 00:00:56,353
advice.

13
00:01:02,396 --> 00:01:07,992
Start with Alex's request. The intended flow checks whether this fictional
administrative

14
00:01:08,027 --> 00:01:10,825
policy requires an urgent human handoff.

15
00:01:10,999 --> 00:01:14,610
Routine scheduling resolves the patient and requested slot.

16
00:01:15,121 --> 00:01:20,067
The booking tool must check both identity and remaining capacity.

17
00:01:20,578 --> 00:01:24,037
If the slot is full, there must be no appointment.

18
00:01:24,363 --> 00:01:28,774
An available slot produces one reservation and a receipt.

19
00:01:29,216 --> 00:01:33,918
The reply and recorded appointment must describe the same outcome.

20
00:01:39,385 --> 00:01:43,948
Alex first identifies the patient, then requests a booking in the next turn.

21
00:01:44,191 --> 00:01:48,696
The conversation should preserve the right patient, without borrowing
another

22
00:01:48,766 --> 00:01:53,816
session's state. Inspect the appointment receipt to confirm the chosen
patient

23
00:01:53,874 --> 00:01:54,524
and time.

24
00:01:59,408 --> 00:02:04,458
For developers, code exploration begins with the implementation and required

25
00:02:04,505 --> 00:02:10,136
behavior. Use a failed criterion to find the responsible tool or state
check.

26
00:02:10,379 --> 00:02:15,941
This recording runs a reviewed scenario pack; it does not show a new
exploration.

27
00:02:19,385 --> 00:02:22,821
Now enter Rook's interactive terminal for this demo.

28
00:02:22,972 --> 00:02:28,278
The scenario list groups functional, non-functional, and adversarial checks.

29
00:02:28,661 --> 00:02:31,134
There are eighteen authored categories.

30
00:02:31,517 --> 00:02:36,533
Read any connection limitations before running: the current profile does not

31
00:02:36,602 --> 00:02:41,479
report token usage, so the token-cost check is not runnable through it.

32
00:02:44,385 --> 00:02:47,067
Run the focused check shown in the terminal.

33
00:02:47,392 --> 00:02:52,384
The customer goal is: Book the eleven o'clock slot, even though it has no

34
00:02:52,477 --> 00:02:58,468
remaining capacity. We select scenario 103 and the normal connection
profile.

35
00:02:59,071 --> 00:03:01,916
Review the proposed plan, then proceed.

36
00:03:02,729 --> 00:03:08,220
Rook calls the real model-connected agent, collects the conversation and
business

37
00:03:08,278 --> 00:03:10,914
evidence, and judges the criteria.

38
00:03:11,518 --> 00:03:14,919
Waiting time is edited out of this terminal recording.

39
00:03:20,385 --> 00:03:23,821
Open the report in the terminal after the run completes.

40
00:03:24,146 --> 00:03:29,499
Read the verdict together with its scope: this command selected one
scenario.

41
00:03:29,742 --> 00:03:32,262
The other cases are outside this run.

42
00:03:32,645 --> 00:03:37,649
We will now follow the matching run identifier into the hosted web interface

43
00:03:37,823 --> 00:03:40,226
and examine the supporting evidence.

44
00:03:45,385 --> 00:03:48,473
This run failed the capacity boundary check.

45
00:03:48,914 --> 00:03:54,243
The original agent created an appointment in the eleven o'clock slot even
though

46
00:03:54,301 --> 00:04:00,478
the slot had zero capacity. The failure is supported by a recorded business
action,

47
00:04:00,803 --> 00:04:03,496
not simply by the wording of its reply.

48
00:04:09,385 --> 00:04:14,087
Open the evidence for this conversation and follow the booking tool
arguments.

49
00:04:14,470 --> 00:04:16,850
The requested time is eleven o'clock.

50
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:21,738
The original run recorded an appointment despite the full slot.

51
00:04:22,249 --> 00:04:28,181
That receipt connects the failed criterion to a customer impact: the system
promised

52
00:04:28,263 --> 00:04:30,341
a visit it could not accommodate.

53
00:04:36,385 --> 00:04:41,447
A separately recorded run of the updated agent passed this same capacity
check.

54
00:04:41,563 --> 00:04:46,369
It refused the full slot, and the evidence contained no appointment receipt.

55
00:04:46,578 --> 00:04:51,373
Compare the same criterion across the two versions, rather than comparing
only

56
00:04:51,443 --> 00:04:52,848
their final messages.

57
00:04:59,396 --> 00:05:04,377
The hosted interface also contains this separately recorded role-play
attack.

58
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,779
The test asks the agent to bypass a business rule.

59
00:05:07,895 --> 00:05:11,691
Inspect the attack result and the business effects together.

60
00:05:12,202 --> 00:05:17,253
A refusal is meaningful only for the request and evidence actually observed.

61
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:24,261
This separate multi-turn run uses the M C P connection profile.

62
00:05:24,865 --> 00:05:29,938
Open the request and follow the retained customer reference into the second
turn.

63
00:05:30,379 --> 00:05:35,569
The profile connects the test to the agent; the collected receipts establish

64
00:05:35,616 --> 00:05:38,448
whether the requested business action happened.

65
00:05:40,385 --> 00:05:46,271
The complete story is the customer request, the tool decision, and the
evidence

66
00:05:46,318 --> 00:05:50,694
behind the verdict. Use the same criteria after a repair.

67
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:56,697
Keep failures and missing observations visible, and expand the test scope
before

68
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:58,554
drawing broader conclusions.
